{"id":"mahabharata-12-250","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":250,"title":"पञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 250 · Death's penance and her task","summary":{"en":"Death, weeping, folds her hands and begs not to be made the slayer of beings, and she goes to the forest to perform severe penance. Brahma at last gives her the task of taking beings at their time, and her tears become the diseases of men.","kn":"ಅಳುತ್ತಿರುವ ಮೃತ್ಯು ಕೈ ಜೋಡಿಸಿ ಜೀವಿಗಳ ಕೊಲೆಗಾರ್ತಿಯಾಗಿಸಬೇಡವೆಂದು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಕಾಡಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಕಠಿಣ ತಪಸ್ಸು ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಕೊನೆಗೆ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಕಾಲ ಬಂದಾಗ ಜೀವಿಗಳನ್ನು ಒಯ್ಯುವ ಕೆಲಸ ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವಳ ಕಣ್ಣೀರು ಮನುಷ್ಯರ ರೋಗಗಳಾಗುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"रोती हुई मृत्यु हाथ जोड़कर विनती करती है कि उसे प्राणियों की हत्यारी न बनाया जाए, और वन जाकर कठोर तप करती है। अन्त में ब्रह्मा उसे काल आने पर प्राणियों को ले जाने का कार्य सौंपते हैं और उसके आँसू मनुष्यों के रोग बन जाते हैं।","te":"ఏడుస్తున్న మృత్యువు చేతులు జోడించి తనను జీవుల హంతకిని చేయవద్దని వేడుకుని అడవికి వెళ్లి కఠిన తపస్సు చేస్తుంది. చివరకు బ్రహ్మ కాలం వచ్చినప్పుడు జీవులను తీసుకెళ్లే పనిని ఇస్తాడు; ఆమె కన్నీళ్లు మనుషుల రోగాలవుతాయి.","ta":"அழும் மரணம் கை கூப்பி உயிர்களைக் கொல்பவளாக்க வேண்டாம் என்று வேண்டி, காட்டுக்குச் சென்று கடுந்தவம் புரிகிறாள். இறுதியில் பிரம்மன் காலம் வரும்போது உயிர்களைக் கொண்டுசெல்லும் பணியை அளிக்கிறான்; அவள் கண்ணீர் மனிதர்களின் நோய்களாகின்றன.","ml":"കരയുന്ന മൃത്യു കൈകൂപ്പി, ജീവികളെ കൊല്ലുന്നവളാക്കരുതെന്ന് അപേക്ഷിക്കുകയും, കഠിനമായ തപസ്സിനായി കാട്ടിൽ പോകുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. ഒടുവിൽ ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അവളെ ജീവികളെ അവരുടെ സമയത്ത് എടുക്കാനുള്ള ചുമതല ഏൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; അവളുടെ കണ്ണീർ മനുഷ്യരുടെ രോഗങ്ങളായി മാറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.250; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विनीय दुःखमबला सा त्वतीवायतेक्षणा ।\nउवाच प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा लतेवावर्जिता तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting down her grief, the woman, her eyes very long, joined her palms and spoke, bowed like a creeper."}},{"n":2,"text":"त्वया सृष्टा कथं नारी मादृशी वदतां वर ।\nरौद्रकर्माभिजायेत सर्वप्राणिभयंकरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of speakers, how can a woman like me, made by you, be born to a dreadful work, terrifying all beings?\""}},{"n":3,"text":"बिभेम्यहमधर्मस्य धर्म्यमादिश कर्म मे ।\nत्वं मां भीतामवेक्षस्व शिवेनेश्वर चक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I fear adharma; give me work that is righteous. Lord, look at me, fearful, with your kind eye.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"बालान्वृद्धान्वयःस्थांश्च न हरेयमनागसः ।\nप्राणिनः प्राणिनामीश नमस्तेऽभिप्रसीद मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I would not take the young, the old or those in their prime who are innocent. Lord of creatures, I bow to you; be gracious to me.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रियान्पुत्रान्वयस्यांश्च भ्रातॄन्मातॄः पितॄनपि ।\nअपध्यास्यन्ति यद्देव मृतांस्तेषां बिभेम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I fear that those whose dear sons, friends, brothers, mothers and fathers die will curse me.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"कृपणाश्रुपरिक्लेदो दहेन्मां शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nतेभ्योऽहं बलवद्भीता शरणं त्वामुपागता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The tears of the wretched would burn me for endless years; I am greatly afraid of them and come to you for refuge.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"यमस्य भवने देव यात्यन्ते पापकर्मिणः ।\nप्रसादये त्वा वरद प्रसादं कुरु मे प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"God, sinners go in the end to Yama's house. Giver of boons, I beg you, be gracious to me, lord.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एतमिच्छाम्यहं कामं त्वत्तो लोकपितामह ।\nइच्छेयं त्वत्प्रसादाच्च तपस्तप्तुं सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I want this wish from you, grandfather of the worlds, and by your grace I wish to practise austerity, lord of the gods.\""}},{"text":"पितामह उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The grandfather said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"मृत्यो संकल्पिता मे त्वं प्रजासंहारहेतुना ।\nगच्छ संहर सर्वास्त्वं प्रजा मा च विचारय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death, you were conceived by me for the sake of destroying creatures; go and destroy all creatures, and do not hesitate."}},{"n":10,"text":"एतदेवमवश्यं हि भविता नैतदन्यथा ।\nक्रियतामनवद्याङ्गि यथोक्तं मद्वचोऽनघे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This must happen so and cannot be otherwise; blameless one, do as I have told you."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"एवमुक्ता महाबाहो मृत्युः परपुरंजय ।\nन व्याजहार तस्थौ च प्रह्वा भगवदुन्मुखी ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, great-armed conqueror of cities, Death did not answer; she stood bowed, facing the god."}},{"n":12,"text":"पुनः पुनरथोक्ता सा गतसत्त्वेव भामिनी ।\nतूष्णीमासीत्ततो देवो देवानामीश्वरेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told again and again, the lady stayed silent as if lifeless. Then the god, lord of the lords of gods,"}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रससाद किल ब्रह्मा स्वयमेवात्मनात्मवान् ।\nस्मयमानश्च लोकेशो लोकान्सर्वानवैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma, self-possessed, himself became gracious, and smiling, the lord of the worlds looked upon all the worlds."}},{"n":14,"text":"निवृत्तरोषे तस्मिंस्तु भगवत्यपराजिते ।\nसा कन्यापजगामास्य समीपादिति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that when the invincible lord's anger ceased, that maiden went away from him."}},{"n":15,"text":"अपसृत्याप्रतिश्रुत्य प्रजासंहरणं तदा ।\nत्वरमाणेव राजेन्द्र मृत्युर्धेनुकमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having left without agreeing to destroy creatures, Death, as if hurried, went to Dhenuka, king of kings."}},{"n":16,"text":"सा तत्र परमं देवी तपोऽचरत दुश्चरम् ।\nसमा ह्येकपदे तस्थौ दश पद्मानि पञ्च च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the goddess practised supreme, hard austerity; she stood on one foot for fifteen padmas of years."}},{"n":17,"text":"तां तथा कुर्वतीं तत्र तपः परमदुश्चरम् ।\nपुनरेव महातेजा ब्रह्मा वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she did that most difficult penance, the radiant Brahma spoke to her again."}},{"n":18,"text":"कुरुष्व मे वचो मृत्यो तदनादृत्य सत्वरा ।\nतथैवैकपदे तात पुनरन्यानि सप्त सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Death, do as I say and do not disregard it.\" But she, my son, again stood on one foot for another seven padmas,"}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्थौ पद्मानि षट्चैव पञ्च द्वे चैव मानद ।\nभूयः पद्मायुतं तात मृगैः सह चचार सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"and six, and five and two, respectful one; then she wandered with deer for ten thousand padmas."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुनर्गत्वा ततो राजन्मौनमातिष्ठदुत्तमम् ।\nअप्सु वर्षसहस्राणि सप्त चैकं च पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, she went again and kept excellent silence in the water for seven thousand and one years."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो जगाम सा कन्या कौशिकीं भरतर्षभ ।\nतत्र वायुजलाहारा चचार नियमं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that maiden went to the Kaushiki, best of Bharatas, and there, living on wind and water, again practised restraint."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो ययौ महाभागा गङ्गां मेरुं च केवलम् ।\nतस्थौ दार्विव निश्चेष्टा भूतानां हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very fortunate one went to the Ganga and Meru alone, and stood motionless like a log, wishing the good of beings."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो हिमवतो मूर्ध्नि यत्र देवाः समीजिरे ।\nतत्राङ्गुष्ठेन राजेन्द्र निखर्वमपरं ततः ।\nतस्थौ पितामहं चैव तोषयामास यत्नतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then on the Himalaya's summit, where the gods once sacrificed, she stood on her big toe for another nikharva, king of kings, and tried hard to please the grandfather."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततस्तामब्रवीत्तत्र लोकानां प्रभवाप्ययः ।\nकिमिदं वर्तते पुत्रि क्रियतां तद्वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the source and end of the worlds said to her, \"What is this you are doing, daughter? Do as I say.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीत्पुनर्मृत्युर्भगवन्तं पितामहम् ।\nन हरेयं प्रजा देव पुनस्त्वाहं प्रसादये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Death spoke again to the venerable grandfather: \"I would not take creatures, god; I beg you again.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"तामधर्मभयत्रस्तां पुनरेव च याचतीम् ।\nतदाब्रवीद्देवदेवो निगृह्येदं वचस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she, afraid of adharma, begged again, the god of gods, restraining her, spoke these words."}},{"n":27,"text":"अधर्मो नास्ति ते मृत्यो संयच्छेमाः प्रजाः शुभे ।\nमया ह्युक्तं मृषा भद्रे भविता नेह किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is no adharma for you, Death; restrain these creatures, fair one. What I have said will not be false, good lady; nothing here will be otherwise.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"धर्मः सनातनश्च त्वामिहैवानुप्रवेक्ष्यते ।\nअहं च विबुधाश्चैव त्वद्धिते निरताः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Eternal dharma will enter you right here, and I and the gods will always be devoted to your good.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"इममन्यं च ते कामं ददामि मनसेप्सितम् ।\nन त्वा दोषेण यास्यन्ति व्याधिसंपीडिताः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I also give you this other wish, desired in your mind: creatures afflicted by disease will not blame you.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"पुरुषेषु च रूपेण पुरुषस्त्वं भविष्यसि ।\nस्त्रीषु स्त्रीरूपिणी चैव तृतीयेषु नपुंसकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Among men you will be male in form, among women of female form, and among the third kind, neuter.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"सैवमुक्ता महाराज कृताञ्जलिरुवाच ह ।\nपुनरेव महात्मानं नेति देवेशमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, great king, she said again with joined palms to the great-souled, imperishable lord of gods: \"No.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"तामब्रवीत्तदा देवो मृत्यो संहर मानवान् ।\nअधर्मस्ते न भविता तथा ध्यास्याम्यहं शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the god said to her, \"Death, destroy humankind. You will have no adharma, and I will think of you, auspicious one.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"यानश्रुबिन्दून्पतितानपश्यं\nये पाणिभ्यां धारितास्ते पुरस्तात् ।\nते व्याधयो मानवान्घोररूपाः\nप्राप्ते काले पीडयिष्यन्ति मृत्यो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The drops of tears that I saw fall, which you held in your hands, those will be diseases, Death, of dreadful form, that will torment men when their time comes.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"सर्वेषां त्वं प्राणिनामन्तकाले\nकामक्रोधौ सहितौ योजयेथाः ।\nएवं धर्मस्त्वामुपैष्यत्यमेयो\nन चाधर्मं लप्स्यसे तुल्यवृत्तिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At the end of life of all creatures, you should join desire and anger together; thus immeasurable dharma will come to you, and, acting impartially, you will gain no adharma.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"एवं धर्मं पालयिष्यस्यथोक्तं\nन चात्मानं मज्जयिष्यस्यधर्मे ।\nतस्मात्कामं रोचयाभ्यागतं त्वं\nसंयोज्याथो संहरस्वेह जन्तून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Thus you will keep dharma as described and will not sink yourself in adharma. Therefore accept the desire that has come, join it and destroy beings here.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"सा वै तदा मृत्युसंज्ञापदेशा-\nच्छापाद्भीता बाढमित्यब्रवीत्तम् ।\nअथो प्राणान्प्राणिनामन्तकाले\nकामक्रोधौ प्राप्य निर्मोह्य हन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, afraid of the curse, called by the name of Death, she said, \"So be it.\" And at the end of life she takes the lives of creatures after confusing them with desire and anger."}},{"n":37,"text":"मृत्योर्ये ते व्याधयश्चाश्रुपाता\nमनुष्याणां रुज्यते यैः शरीरम् ।\nसर्वेषां वै प्राणिनां प्राणनान्ते\nतस्माच्छोकं मा कृथा बुध्य बुद्ध्या ॥","meaning":{"en":"The diseases of Death, which are her tears, by which men's bodies suffer at the end of the breath of all creatures, are as I said; so do not grieve; understand with your intellect."}},{"n":38,"text":"सर्वे देवाः प्राणिनां प्राणनान्ते\nगत्वा वृत्ताः संनिवृत्तास्तथैव ।\nएवं सर्वे मानवाः प्राणनान्ते\nगत्वावृत्ता देववद्राजसिंह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the gods, at the end of creatures' lives, go, live and return in the same way; so all humans, at the end of their breath, go and return like gods, lion among kings."}},{"n":39,"text":"वायुर्भीमो भीमनादो महौजाः\nसर्वेषां च प्राणिनां प्राणभूतः ।\nनानावृत्तिर्देहिनां देहभेदे\nतस्माद्वायुर्देवदेवो विशिष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wind is terrible, of fearful roar, of great might, the very breath of all creatures; in the various activities of embodied beings, at the separation of the body, so the wind is the superior god of gods."}},{"n":40,"text":"सर्वे देवा मर्त्यसंज्ञाविशिष्टाः\nसर्वे मर्त्या देवसंज्ञाविशिष्टाः ।\nतस्मात्पुत्रं मा शुचो राजसिंह\nपुत्रः स्वर्गं प्राप्य ते मोदते ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All gods are distinguished by the name \"mortal,\" and all mortals by the name \"god.\" So do not grieve for your son, lion among kings; your son has reached heaven and rejoices."}},{"n":41,"text":"एवं मृत्युर्देवसृष्टा प्रजानां\nप्राप्ते काले संहरन्ती यथावत् ।\nतस्याश्चैव व्याधयस्तेऽश्रुपाताः\nप्राप्ते काले संहरन्तीह जन्तून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus Death, made by the god, destroys creatures properly when their time comes, and her diseases, the tears, destroy creatures here when their time comes."}}]}]}